      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Preemptive strikes against authoritarian regimes are morally justified only when there is an imminent, specific threat of mass atrocities that cannot be stopped by diplomacy, as seen in the clear cases of preventing genocide. A democratic nation has a moral obligation to protect human life and uphold international law, which includes the right to self-defense against imminent aggression. Therefore, if an authoritarian regime is actively preparing for an attack that will cause widespread suffering, a preemptive strike is not only ethical but a necessary act of moral responsibility.",
