      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to be skeptical, because history is littered with powerful nations using \"imminent threat\" as a convenient excuse for imperial overreach and unchecked warfare. A truly robust moral framework must include strict, objective criteria—such as a clear, imminent threat of mass atrocities and the exhaustion of all diplomatic avenues—to prevent powerful democracies from simply projecting their own biases onto other nations. Without these rigorous constraints, the principle of non-intervention becomes a dangerous shield for tyranny, but without the threat of intervention, the world risks descending into a state of constant, unchecked warfare where the weak are left to suffer.",
      "source": "target",
